                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote14" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 14"><sup>14</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>For more on Penn-Central, see Charles Calomiris, &ldquo;<a href="https://research.stlouisfed.org/publications/review/article/3141">Is the Discount Window Necessary? A Penn-Central Perspective</a>,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis <em>Review</em>, May/June 1994, vol. 76, no. 3, pp. 31-56.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote15" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 15"><sup>15</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>See Irving H. Sprague, &ldquo;<em>Bailout: An Insider&rsquo;s Account of Bank Failures and Rescues,&rdquo;</em> Washington D.C.: Beard Books, 1986.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote16" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 16"><sup>16</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Gary H. Stern and Ron J. Feldman, <em>Too Big to Fail: The Hazards of Bank Bailouts</em>, Washington, D.C.: Brookings Institution Press, 2004, p. 31.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote17" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 17"><sup>17</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>For more on the debate about deposit insurance, see Mark D. Flood, &ldquo;<a href="http://research.stlouisfed.org/publications/review/92/07/Deposit_Jul_Aug1992.pdf" target="_blank">The Great Deposit Insurance Debate</a>,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis <em>Review</em>, July/August 1992, vol. 74, no. 4, pp. 51-77; and Charles Calomiris, &ldquo;<a href="http://web.mit.edu/14.71/www/Calomiris%20deposit%20insurance.pdf" target="_blank">Is Deposit Insurance Necessary? A Historical Perspective</a>,&rdquo; <em>The Journal of Economic History</em>, June 1990, vol. 50, no. 2, pp. 283-295.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote18" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 18"><sup>18</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>For more on living wills, see Arantxa Jarque and David A. Price, &ldquo;<a href="/-/media/RichmondFedOrg/publications/research/annual_report/2014/pdf/article.pdf">Living Wills: A Tool for Curbing &lsquo;Too Big to Fail&rsquo;</a>,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond 2014 <em>Annual Report</em>, May 2015.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote19" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 19"><sup>19</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Marvin Goodfriend, &ldquo;<a href="http://ideas.repec.org/a/ime/imemes/v30y2012p39-54.html" target="_blank">The Elusive Promise of Independent Central Banking</a>,&rdquo; <em>Monetary and Economic Studies</em>, Institute for Monetary and Economic Studies, Bank of Japan, November 2012, vol. 30, pp. 39-54.</p></div>
                </div>
    </div>
    <script>
        window.addEventListener('load', function (event) {
            // footnotesInit() is default export from footnotes.es6.js
            footnotesInit();

        });
    </script>
